Note: @generative stdlib module
Note: Markov chain primitive in BOTH one-shot AND train+generate-split
Note: shapes. First-class MarkovModel reference-identity value type —
Note: see CLAUDE.md Music Types Quick Reference table.

module generative

Note: One-shot — compose train + generate at the call site
internal proc markov (Sequence: corpus, Int: order, Int: length, Int: seed)
internal proc markov (Sequence: corpus, Int: order, Int: length)
Note: Array-corpus forms (0615) — train directly off a Note[] or Int[] of
Note: pitches without first wrapping them in a Sequence. Int elements are raw
Note: MIDI pitches; Note elements parse their note string. Same pitch-feature
Note: Markov path, so determinism + the train/generate split are byte-identical.
internal proc markov (Note[]: corpus, Int: order, Int: length, Int: seed)
internal proc markov (Note[]: corpus, Int: order, Int: length)
internal proc markov (Int[]: corpus, Int: order, Int: length, Int: seed)
internal proc markov (Int[]: corpus, Int: order, Int: length)

Note: Train once / generate many
internal proc markovTrain (Sequence: corpus, Int: order)
Note: features= accepts Symbol (e.g. #pitch) or Tuple<<Symbol, Symbol>>
Note: (e.g. <<#pitch, #duration>>) — the Void wildcard slot dispatches at runtime.
internal proc markovTrain (Sequence: corpus, Int: order, Void: features)
Note: Array-corpus train forms (0615) — mirror the one-shot array surface.
internal proc markovTrain (Note[]: corpus, Int: order)
internal proc markovTrain (Int[]: corpus, Int: order)

internal proc markovGenerate (MarkovModel: model, Int: length, Int: seed)
internal proc markovGenerate (MarkovModel: model, Int: length)

Note: Structural compare — distinct from (eq m1 m2), which is reference identity.
internal proc markovEqual (MarkovModel: a, MarkovModel: b)

Note: L-system primitive.
Note: Pure deterministic Symbol rewriting; iteration count clamped to [0, 20]
Note: as a DoS guard. Rule values accept Tuple<<Symbol, ...>>
Note: (the canonical composer surface) or Symbol[] — the C# registration uses
Note: Dict<Void, Void> as a wildcard so EITHER value-shape resolves; the proc
Note: decl annotates the most-common composer surface (Symbol[]) but the
Note: wildcard registration in LsystemFunctions.cs:RegisterContextDependent
Note: accepts tuple-valued dicts equally.
internal proc lsystem (Symbol: axiom, Dict<Symbol, Symbol[]>: rules, Int: iterations)
internal proc lsystemModel (Symbol: axiom, Dict<Symbol, Symbol[]>: rules)
internal proc lsystemGenerate (LsystemModel: model, Int: iterations)
internal proc lsystemToSequence (Symbol[]: expanded, Function: mapper)
internal proc lsystemEqual (LsystemModel: a, LsystemModel: b)

Note: Cellular automata primitives.
Note: 1D `cellular` uses the Wolfram-convention single-1-center default seed
Note: pattern; the seed arg is accepted for signature uniformity but ignored.
Note: `cellularSeeded` accepts an explicit Array[Bool] initial pattern.
Note: 2D `life` uses a composer-supplied seed to seed a Random for 30%-density
Note: initial fill. Both 1D and 2D primitives clamp width/height/steps to
Note: <= 1024 (DoS guard) and wrap rule values via & 0xFF.
internal proc cellular (Int: rule, Int: width, Int: steps, Int: seed)
internal proc cellularSeeded (Int: rule, Int: width, Int: steps, Int: seed, Bool[]: initialPattern)
internal proc life (Int: width, Int: height, Int: steps, Int: seed)

Note: Chaos-map primitives.
Note: Lorenz attractor (forward-Euler with σ=10, ρ=28, β=8/3 canonical
Note: butterfly) and logistic map (x_{n+1} = r * x_n * (1 - x_n)) both
Note: return raw Array[Double]; composer quantizes to musical pitch via
Note: (quantizeToScale series scale). length is clamped to <= 100_000
Note: (DoS guard). Cross-platform FP divergence is a known limitation —
Note: same-platform two-run cmp-clean is preserved (single-machine IEEE
Note: 754 reproducibility); cross-platform reproducibility is NOT
Note: guaranteed for the chaotic-system outputs of these primitives.
internal proc lorenz (Double: sigma, Double: rho, Double: beta, Int: length, Int: seed)
internal proc logistic (Double: r, Int: length, Int: seed)
Note: quantizeToScale ships in two overloads:
Note: a String-form that resolves a scale name via ScaleDatabase, and an
Note: Array[Note] form that lets composers supply the scale directly.
internal proc quantizeToScale (Double[]: series, String: scaleName)
internal proc quantizeToScale (Double[]: series, Note[]: scaleNotes)
